# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan gate (scripts/asan_check.sh).
#
# Only library-internal retention that the framework cannot control belongs here,
# plus allocations the framework retains ON PURPOSE with the decision written down
# next to it in the code (see the entry below). Anything the framework allocates
# and simply fails to release must stay reported, so keep this file minimal and
# justify every entry.
#
# A suppression hides a whole class of reports at once, so an entry is only
# acceptable when the code says why the memory is still there; "it is only a few
# bytes" is not a reason.

# libfontconfig keeps its parsed font configuration (320 B) allocated after Qt's
# QFontDatabase initialization and never releases it at exit. The allocation is
# reachable only from the library's own static state; the framework neither
# created nor holds it.
leak:libfontconfig
leak:libexpat

# The plugin loader's libraries and its bookkeeping (a map of DynamicLibrary
# handles, one per plugin) are retained DELIBERATELY. ~DynamicLibraryLoader
# releases its impl instead of destroying it, because destroying it would dlclose
# the loaded plugins during static destruction -- and the process-wide registries
# (CommandManager, RenderBackendRegistry) are destroyed in an order relative to
# that, while still holding callables and factory pointers INTO the plugin code,
# so unmapping it first segfaults on exit. The reasoning, and what a future
# unload implementation must do instead, is written next to that release() in
# src/base/runtime/src/DynamicLibraryLoader.cpp.
#
# Measured (2026-09-16): this is the ONLY leak a test_vsg run reports -- 808 B in
# 16 allocations, all in vn::runtime::DynamicLibraryLoader /
# DynamicLibrary::DynamicLibrary, with no frame in the vsg backend. Before this
# entry, the backend's ASan run had to be judged with VINE_ASAN_LEAK_SCOPE (report
# leaks outside a pattern without failing); with it, the whole suite runs with
# plain all-or-nothing leak judging, which is the stronger setting.
leak:vn::runtime::DynamicLibrary
